When the forward kinematics of a hexapod fails, motion must start the next
forward from the last pose it had, not from home.  An iterative forward
started at home far from the joints can converge to another platform pose
with the same strut lengths, and stays on it from then on.

The platform is moved far from home, and genhexkins.limit-iterations is
set to 0 for a few cycles so the forward fails; then the feedback position,
and in joint mode the commanded position, must be where the platform is.
